<?php
/**
 * Spartrak — the cart's `الشحن الي` row, and the page's checkout config.
 *
 * FIGMA SSOT: 553:4765 (desktop) / 675:17361 (mobile). A 56px white disc at the
 * reading start, `الشحن الي` and the shopper's address beside it. One row, 88
 * tall, and nothing behind it.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * THE SHIPPING-AND-TAX ESTIMATOR IS GONE. THE CONFIG IT SAT ON IS NOT.
 * ===========================================================================
 * Core's cart/shipping.phtml renders two things that have nothing to do with
 * each other beyond sharing a file:
 *
 *   1. `#block-summary` — a Knockout scope holding `تقدير الشحن والضرائب`: a
 *      country select, a governorate select, a postcode box and the shipping
 *      -rate radios, behind a collapsible chevron.
 *   2. `window.checkoutConfig` — the quote, the totals, the price format and
 *      the customer, published as a global.
 *
 * ONLY THE FIRST IS REMOVED. Figma's cart has no estimator: 553:4762 is the
 * ship-to row, the totals card and the instalments panel, full stop. The
 * shopper's governorate already decides the rate, they are one button from a
 * checkout that asks for it properly, and the estimator's own markup came up
 * in English ("Enter your destination to get a shipping estimate.") because it
 * is copy this store never translated. Removing it also stops four Knockout
 * components, a directory-region payload and a rate lookup from booting on a
 * page that does not use them (CLAUDE.md sections 4 and 13).
 *
 * THE SECOND HAS TO STAY, and this is the whole reason the block is still here
 * rather than removed in layout XML. The cart's totals are core's Knockout
 * components; `Magento_Checkout/js/model/quote` reads `window.checkoutConfig`
 * at module load and throws without it. Delete the script and the summary
 * column renders empty. It is published from this template because this is
 * where core publishes it, and moving it would only mean owning the ordering
 * question as well.
 *
 * `getJsLayout()` is deliberately never called now, so core's estimator
 * jsLayout is built and then not used — the block keeps the argument for any
 * extension that reads it, and this page pays nothing to render it.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * NO ADDRESS, NO ROW
 * ===========================================================================
 * The design draws no empty state, so a shopper with no saved address does not
 * see the row. It is now genuinely skipped rather than hidden with a modifier
 * class: with the estimator gone, the row and the script are independent, so
 * omitting one no longer risks the other.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * NONE OF CORE'S CLASS NAMES SURVIVE, ON PURPOSE
 * ===========================================================================
 * `.block.shipping` and `.title` are Porto/blank hooks. They brought a border,
 * a page-block margin and a `::after` chevron of their own to a row Figma
 * draws as a flat two-line label — the hairline under `الشحن الي` was that
 * border. Overriding them with `border: none` would have been a fourth rule
 * fighting three; not wearing the classes means there is nothing to fight
 * (CLAUDE.md sections 2 and 9).
 *
 * @var \Magento\Checkout\Block\Cart\Shipping $block
 * @var \Magento\Framework\Escaper $escaper
 * @var \Magento\Framework\View\Helper\SecureHtmlRenderer $secureRenderer
 */

/** @var \Spartrak\Checkout\ViewModel\CartShipTo $shipTo */
$shipTo = $block->getData('ship_to_view_model');
?>
<?php if ($shipTo !== null && $shipTo->hasAddress()): ?>
    <?php /* Core wore `role="heading" aria-level="2"` here because the element
             LABELLED the estimator region below it — that is what
             `aria-labelledby="block-shipping-heading"` pointed at. With the
             region gone the role would be a heading that labels nothing and
             announces an address, which puts a street name into the document
             outline and into every screen reader's heading list.

             So it is a plain label/value pair now. `<dl>` was the other
             candidate and is rejected for the same reason the row is a grid:
             one term and one description is a list of one, and the extra
             wrapper buys nothing the two spans do not already say. */ ?>
    <div class="spartrak-cart-shipto">
        <span class="spartrak-cart-shipto__label">
            <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Shipping to')) ?>
        </span>
        <span class="spartrak-cart-shipto__address">
            <?= $escaper->escapeHtml($shipTo->getAddressLine()) ?>
        </span>
    </div>
<?php endif; ?>
<?php
$serializedCheckoutConfig = /* @noEscape */ $block->getSerializedCheckoutConfig();

$scriptString = <<<script

            window.checkoutConfig = {$serializedCheckoutConfig};
            window.customerData = window.checkoutConfig.customerData;
            window.isCustomerLoggedIn = window.checkoutConfig.isCustomerLoggedIn;
            require([
                'mage/url',
                'Magento_Ui/js/block-loader'
            ], function(url, blockLoader) {
                blockLoader(
                    "{$block->escapeJs($block->escapeUrl($block->getViewFileUrl('images/loader-1.gif')))}"
                );
                return url.setBaseUrl('{$block->escapeJs($block->escapeUrl($block->getBaseUrl()))}');
            })
script;
?>
<?= /* @noEscape */ $secureRenderer->renderTag('script', [], $scriptString, false) ?>
